No, i'm not proposing a new kind of monster, i just thought i'd post a few
minor bugs while nh3.0 is in the works. These things have probably been noticed
by many people, but may not have been made public before.

When something is engraved on the floor and an object is on that spot, you see
the writing on the floor, then the object, then the writing on the floor again.

When you engrave something, then later eat something, then when you finish
eating, the message says something like `You finish engraving.' This may only
occur under limited circumstances; i'm not sure exactly.

When you pray and you are wearing a cursed ring or rings, the message says
`Your left [or right] hand amber' instead of `... glows amber.' Also, when you
throw some kind of food at a wild dog that the dog won't eat (like fruit, i
think) the dog will not attack but will also not follow you; this is fine, but
then when you bump into the dog, you get a message like `Really attack the
@#S3%% ?'. At least these are the circumstances under which i remember
experiencing this garbled message.

One other plea for nh3.0: please, please, please make the dog get out of the
player's way after being bumped into. This is one of the most annoying features
of the game for me - bumping into the dog two dozen times in a long hallway.
Maybe there should be a #talk command which would allow a player with a few
tripe rations to teach his dog some tricks (like staying out of the player's
way (heel), stay, etc.).

